<title>UK: BADMINTON-ARBI MOVES UP IN WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>BADMINTON-ARBI MOVES UP IN WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former world champion Heryanto</p>
<p>Arbi of Indonesia, winner of the singles title at the Konica Cup</p>
<p>Singapore Open on Sunday, moves up four places to second spot in</p>
<p>the world rankings issued on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Arbi, who lost his title in Glasgow in May, recorded his</p>
<p>second grand prix success of the season which followed victory</p>
<p>at the Indian Open in February.</p>
<p>Dong Jiong of China, despite his absence from Singapore,</p>
<p>maintains a clear lead at the top of the standings.</p>
<p>Mia Audina's win over Gong Zhichao in the women's final, was</p>
<p>enough to lift her two places to number four but Ye Zhaoying of</p>
<p>China remains unchallenged at the top.</p>
<p>Leading rankings:</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>  1. Dong Jiong  (China)		  308.60 points</p>
<p>  2. Heryanto Arbi (Indonesia)	  284.40</p>
<p>  3. Sun Jun (China)			268.76</p>
<p>  4. Joko Suprianto (Indonesia)	 264.42</p>
<p>  5. Park Sung-woo (South Korea)	260.25</p>
<p>6. Poul-Erik Hoyer-Larsen (Denmark) 260.23</p>
<p>  7. Peter Rasmussen (Denmark)	  254.53</p>
<p>  8. Ardy B. Wiranata (Indonesia)     236.80</p>
<p>  9. Indra Wijaya (Indonesia)	   226.08</p>
<p>10. Thomas Stuer-Lauridsen (Denmark) 220.56</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p>  1. Ye Zhaoying  (China)		 352.28</p>
<p>  2. Susi Susanti (Indonesia)	   330.45</p>
<p>  3. Gong Zhichao (China)		 305.52</p>
<p>  4. Mia Audina (Indonesia)	     287.38</p>
<p>  5. Wang Chen (China)		    277.22</p>
<p>  6. Camilla Martin (Denmark)	   269.92</p>
<p>  7. Zhang Ning  (China)		  255.85</p>
<p>  8. Dai Yun  (China)		     236.03</p>
<p>  9. Kim Ji-hyun (South Korea)	  234.19</p>
<p> 10. Ra Kyung-min (South Korea)	 230.30</p>
<p>Next event: Russian Open, Moscow, August 26-31.</p>
</text>
